<mxCell id="fnote" parent="1" style="text;html=1;fontSize=11;fontColor=#4A5563;align=left;fontStyle=2;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="FK partner_id (vendor_profiles, pur_rfx_invitations, pur_order_hdrs, pur_contract_hdrs) references CRM.partners.id — cross-schema, Core-peer read, no local edge drawn (Purchase never writes into CRM). FK document_id (pur_vendor_documents, pur_receipt_lines.photo_document_id, pur_contract_hdrs) references a DMS-managed document — no local edge. inventory_goods_receipt_id (pur_receipt_hdrs) is an informational reference to INVENTORY.goods_receipts.id, not an enforced FK, since Inventory is an optional install (PURCHASE_SPECS.md §3E/§5) — no edge drawn. requester_id/receiver_id/assigned_by-style user references point to Laravel&#39;s own users table, outside this schema — no edge drawn. Payment/AP recording is NOT modeled here: a matched invoice fires BillRequested into ACCOUNTING.ap_bills, which owns the payable ledger from that point (§3F/§5) — deliberately no local pur_payments table. Future Version-only tables (pur_rfx_criteria/scorecards, pur_capa_records, pur_audit_records, pur_esg_scores, pur_supplier_scorecards) are omitted per the MVP-first bias stated in §2/§5." vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="1652" width="1750" height="100" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
